{"type":"assistant","sessionId":"session_005","timestamp":"2026-07-29T17:26:19.089Z","cwd":"/project/src/file1","message":{"role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the full info on **Speak-to-AI** (now renamed to **Dabri**):\n\n## 1. GitHub Repository URL\n\n**Original (renamed):** `https://project/src/file10` — the project was renamed from \"speak-to-ai\" to **Dabri** in v2.0.1 (May 2025).  \n**Fork preserving the old name:** `https://project/src/file7`\n\n## 2. AppImage & Flatpak\n\n**Both are available.**  \n- **AppImage** — downloaded from Releases, portable  \n- **Flatpak** — Flathub-ready since v2.1.2, bundles the small Whisper model so voice typing works out of the box\n\nAlso available via **AUR** (`dabri`) and **Fedora COPR** (`ashbuk/dabri`).\n\n## 3. Installation for Ubuntu (Ubuntu 22.04+)\n\n```bash\n# Download latest AppImage from releases:\nwget https://project/src/file11*.AppImage\nchmod +x dabri-*.AppImage\n# Add user to input group for hotkeys:\nsudo usermod -a -G input $USER\n# Logout/login, then run:\n./dabri-*.AppImage\n```\n\nUbuntu 22.04+, Linux Mint 21+, Pop!_OS 22.04+, Elementary OS 7+, Zorin OS 17+ are officially supported.\n\n## 4. Wayland Support\n\n**Yes.** The app explicitly supports both X11 and Wayland:\n- Uses **wtype** for Wayland typing (auto-detected)\n- Uses **xdg-desktop-portal** for global shortcuts on GNOME/Wayland\n- Falls back to clipboard mode if direct typing isn't available\n- Wayland portal typing handles Unicode via auto-paste (v2.2.0)\n\n## 5. Chinese Language Support\n\n**Yes.** The app advertises \"Multi-language support\" and uses **Whisper models** (base/project/src/file12) which natively support Chinese (Mandarin/Cantonese) speech recognition. You can switch models via tray or CLI. No separate language pack needed — Whisper handles Chinese out of the box."}]}}
